WEBVTT

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:18.170
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.750
Kumo to kumo amime o nukete

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.290
Odoru hane kaze o matou

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.750
Me no mae de hoshi ga ochiteiku

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.040
Akogareta aoi ao

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.080
Nijimu chihyou keriageta

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:47.290
Kikasete yo kimi dake no sora no ne o

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:56.630
Tobidatsu jyuuryoku o mikata ni tsukete

00:00:56.750 --> 00:01:03.040
Mou ichido nando demo warai nagara

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:10.080
Bokura wa ushiro o muite tobou to wa shinai

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:15.290
Tsukinai yume asu o otte ikiru

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.790
Waita zetsubou ni ai o tozashita

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:21.080
Yowai boku wa kirai da

00:01:21.790 --> 00:01:27.040
Nagareru ima mukau saki wa mirai

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.940
No Place to Return

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.540
Cut it out! Malo's a good boy!

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.040
Quit it!

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.130
You're a real pain in the butt, you know!

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.290
Well, I suppose we should have expected mister big
shot Isao to be the center of attention.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:55.760
But we shot down one of those Hiryu!

00:01:55.760 --> 00:02:00.050
I do say we deserve at least a bit
more recognition for our deeds than this.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:03.500
Oh yes, I heard Reona was 
really something out there.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:04.330
Nah...

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.630
Sure would have loved to see that
again for a change, right Anna?

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.290
The old "Tenacious Reona".

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:11.250
Don't go imagining things. I 
didn't do anything out there.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.210
If anything I just got in the way...

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.460
Oh listen to you, captain!

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.580
Always so modest.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:16.270
No, I honestly have a lot to reflect on,

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.500
both as captain, and as a 
fighter pilot to begin with.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.710
It's unthinkable how I could just get so swept away
that I would break formation like that.

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:23.210
I'm really sorry about it all.

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.040
I swear I will make up 
for these blunders some-

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.120
Some might call that a debt in and of itself.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.330
What good would it do you 
to be indebted again?

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.710
Reona, you're the captain of this squad.
Let your team help you.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.290
The Madame's right, you know.

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.460
We'd all love it if you did.

00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.720
And quit getting all worked up
about owing anyone anything.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.330
Can't we just work together, 
no strings attached?

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.180
I'll... see what I can do.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.390
You can start by lending me some cash!

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.290
I need to get Malo-chan a wife!

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:49.080
A "wife"?

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:50.580
Is that thing male?

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.900
Well duh!

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.380
So lend me some dough, no strings attached!

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:55.250
Not going to happen.

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.310
And here I was, thinking 
the team might help me out!

00:02:57.310 --> 00:03:01.080
I myself am quite against procuring
a spouse for that anomalocaris.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:03.590
Whenever I make eye contact 
with that doll late at night

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.650
I fear my heart might simply stop dead.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:06.500
That's so mean!

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.580
I'm sure Kylie feels quite the same.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.540
That's three to one, it is.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:11.750
But Kylie...

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:14.210
...would probably say no, huh?

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.420
I wonder what that girl is up to right now.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.740
I should have been the one to handle this.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:22.760
When you're dealing with someone like Julia,
Kylie is much more suited to the job.

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:29.850
That numbskull! Look at 
him all full of himself!

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:31.880
"Like riding a bike"?

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:33.210
Don't make me laugh!

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.080
Uhh...

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.830
And now these old geezers in Gadoll

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:39.440
who had never given Ikesuka the time 
of day are suddenly flip-flopping.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.790
If you can't beat them, join them, is it?

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.920
They're always ever so quick to pander.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:44.990
Can you please pay us?

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:45.880
Pay you?

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:47.460
For defending Areshima.

00:03:47.460 --> 00:03:50.000
It's all right there on 
that invoice I gave you.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.420
I was hoping Loulou would be here so I could 
get her to cut some of these zeroes off...

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:54.040
Huh?

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.080
No, never you mind.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:57.710
All of this?

00:03:57.710 --> 00:04:00.280
I would never deny anyone the 
chance to call me wicked,

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.840
but I won't have anyone 
accuse me of being stingy.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.140
Don't go dropping that, now.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.250
I-I'd never!

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:08.790
Oh, hey, Miss Julia?

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.580
What is it?

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.250
What happens now?

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:15.740
Are we really going to be left grounded until
we submit papers and get granted permission?

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:20.670
And are they gonna be deciding who can and
can't fly and hand out licenses and stuff?

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.050
All because there are more 
and more of these pricks

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:25.280
who just want to bend the 
world to their whims.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:27.780
You're either an idiot who joins them,
or a fool that doesn't.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.200
Those are the only two choices.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:53.960
You egging me on?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.210
Having a laugh at me?
Looking for a fight?

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.920
Well I'm down for it!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.420
I sure hope you weren't 
thinking you could lose me!

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.210
First Officer, we are hitting altitudes
well above our observed altitude.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:09.750
We're looking at explosive cyclogenesis.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:12.470
It might be best to situate 
the Hagoromo elsewhere.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.130
What? That sounds like a huge pain.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:17.920
You sure we can't just ignore it all?

00:06:18.500 --> 00:06:20.710
Okay, I'll do it! I swear!

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:23.290
We're in for it. A real big one.

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.290
Batten down the hatch!

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:25.420
Lock those fighters in place!

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.010
If any of them get so much 
as a scratch I'm gonna

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.840
tie you up like a windsock up atop this ship!

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:30.000
Roger!
By all means!

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:41.420
Don't think I forgot about 
the time you shot me down!

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.340
Or how you came out of 
nowhere back in Porokka!

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.260
Or when you came in with all those air pirates
on the way back from Shouto!

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:02.880
Quit running and fight me!

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.130
They didn't shoot? Why?

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:32.880
Why you little...!

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.800
Don't even think I'm worth your time, huh?!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:35.750
I'll show you!

00:07:57.700 --> 00:07:58.670
You're not getting away!

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:06.540
Chika, can you quit fidgeting like that?

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.170
I'm not fidgeting, okay?

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.250
I can hardly even concentrate 
on my calculations here.

00:09:10.250 --> 00:09:16.170
Emma, that shouldn't be 21 pounds and 45 sen,
but 23 pounds and 55 sen.

00:09:16.710 --> 00:09:17.920
Well, thank you for pointing that out.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:20.000
I hate these low-pressure areas.

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:22.460
It makes my head feel all woozy.

00:09:22.460 --> 00:09:24.290
I think you've just drank too much.

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.210
I know the difference between being drunk
and the feel of low-pressure.

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:27.870
Do you really, now?

00:09:27.870 --> 00:09:29.750
When is she gonna get back?

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:30.750
She won't be returning.

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:31.420
What?!

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:34.310
We can assume she has fled for safety from

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:36.280
the storm much like the Hagoromo has.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:37.500
True, yeah.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:41.170
You don't think...

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:42.080
Stop.

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:44.170
Not one more word, Zara.

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.540
Never mind, then.

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.380
Never mind what?

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.210
Kylie's coming back, right?

00:09:51.630 --> 00:09:53.170
One thing I know for sure...

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:56.380
Chika's worried about Kylie.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.630
Oh.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.420
Understood.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:10:01.000
Nuh-uh! It's the money! I'm 
worried about the money!

00:10:01.380 --> 00:10:02.960
Hey! Are you dead?

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:07.380
I... was shot down.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.630
The money...

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:10.750
...is still there.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:27.750
The whole top half of my 
engine is blown to bits.

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:29.670
Fuel tank is still in tact.

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:32.790
Natsuo did say it was leak 
resistant now that I think of it.

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:35.670
The radio's out, and for some reason
my landing gear is deployed.

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:37.130
Did I do that?

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.500
When did I pull that off?

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:40.250
Was it just muscle memory?

00:10:40.250 --> 00:10:41.540
Did my subconscious do it all for me?

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:03.160
No doubt about it, this is Ofukouyama.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:07.040
In Yufang, they have ships out at sea
instead of in the skies, right?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:12.580
Ofukouyama is supposed to be the same size
as one of their ship's runways.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:17.730
So all the new pilot recruits 
go there to practice.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:21.210
And they came up with all sorts of ways to make
shorter landings and stuff.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:26.330
But no matter what nothing worked out,
and it was nothing but a disaster.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.960
The name Ofukouyama even means disaster!

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:30.130
Isn't that right, Ol' Sab?

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:34.210
Rahama is exactly 260 kilometers 
away flying straight.

00:11:34.210 --> 00:11:37.300
And there's not a single 
airfield or town in between.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:42.240
Forever and ever ago,
there used to be something here, though.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.630
That stinking So-un Ravine 
is what's really in my way.

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:46.960
I can't even get off Ofukouyama.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:48.500
Even if I did I'd just wind up in the ravine.

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:51.250
So I've gotta do something 
about my engine, here.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:57.940
Shot down yet again...

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.940
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:01.630
Are you dead?

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:04.080
No, I'm quite alive.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:07.420
Aww, shucks. I thought I'd get 
to see my first real corpse.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:10.130
You've never seen one?

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.790
Nope. Not a nice fresh dead one.

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:13.750
Well, sorry to disappoint.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.630
Can you grab me that bag?

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.210
Shouldn't you be getting back?

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:23.040
Back where?

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.750
Home. Everyone must be worried.

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:28.530
It's fine. Someone's probably 
eating my dinner anyway.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:29.930
We always fight over our food.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.210
Aren't you afraid?

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:33.130
Of what?

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:34.040
Of me.

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.310
I know who you are!

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.540
And how you live on the 
outskirts of Shioyama.

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:40.420
How you come around to 
buy gasoline from Sunami.

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:42.790
And how everyone calls you "Ol' Sab"!

00:12:43.130 --> 00:12:45.170
Yeah, that's all well and true.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:48.800
If I were to add anything 
else it'd be that I'm a

00:12:48.800 --> 00:12:50.920
reclusive, murderous, hot-tempered fugitive.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:51.580
What...?

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.130
Now, run along home.

00:12:53.130 --> 00:12:56.040
What'd you do, Ol' Sab? 
You're a real fugitive?!

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:57.790
Listen, kid...

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.920
I'm not "kid", I'm Kylie!

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:11.210
Dangit...

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:13.960
Does it hurt?

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:16.000
Want some water?

00:13:16.630 --> 00:13:17.210
Quiet, you.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:17.790
But...

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:19.330
Enough! Get lost!

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:26.080
Yoshi's field got hit again.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:27.250
Again? You're kidding!

00:13:27.250 --> 00:13:30.880
If you ask me, I say it's that
Shioyama fella who's up to no good.

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:31.830
Ol' Sab?

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:32.420
Yeah.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:33.710
I should have known.

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:36.410
What do you expect from a guy abandoned
by the rest of Yufang?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:38.420
Ol' Sab is from Yufang?

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:41.290
That's no concern for children like you!

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.380
Go on, get outta here.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:47.880
Oh, you're still alive.

00:13:51.710 --> 00:13:52.540
Kid...

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:52.750
Locomotives

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.500
I'm not "kid", I'm Kylie!

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.960
Ol' Sab, are you from Yufang?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.130
And what if I am?

00:13:59.790 --> 00:14:02.380
You Yufang people came to 
Ijitsu from that hole, right?

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:04.080
Flying in on your planes?

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:08.130
Then you built tons of factories,
and made lots of airplanes.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:09.170
Yeah...

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:12.710
But one day you all just 
left back through that hole.

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:17.380
Leaving your factories, your airplanes,
and everything here in Ijitsu.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:20.140
And then the hole disappeared.

00:14:20.140 --> 00:14:22.460
Why didn't you go back home?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.040
Did you oversleep?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.290
Who knows?

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:26.880
Maybe you had a tummy-ache?

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:27.880
Maybe.

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:32.960
I'm back!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.540
Look what I found!

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.170
This is Yufang-ese, right?

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.250
What does it say?

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:38.830
Beats me.

00:14:38.830 --> 00:14:39.920
Tell me!

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.700
S-so you see, I was just 
trying to grab a book, see?

00:14:56.700 --> 00:14:59.090
And the whole thing just came crumbling down!

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:03.380
Are you really not afraid of me?

00:15:03.380 --> 00:15:05.000
Nope! You're fun!

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:06.090
"Fun"?

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:12.670
You got all sorts of who knows what here,
and you know lots about stuff!

00:15:13.130 --> 00:15:14.050
So you're just real fun!

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:16.880
Where were you before you came to Rahama?

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:19.000
Are there really mountains 
taller than Shioyama?

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:20.750
Have you ever seen the sea or even a lake?

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.130
Can you eat fish?

00:15:22.130 --> 00:15:22.960
Have you eaten any?

00:15:22.960 --> 00:15:23.580
Are they yummy?

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:25.210
Are you really from Yufang?

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.040
Why does that matter to you?

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.670
Hm? "Why?"

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:32.830
Well, I just wanna know what I don't know!

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:34.330
I've never seen any of 
that sort of stuff before.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.380
So I wanna know about it. I wanna see it!

00:15:37.210 --> 00:15:38.910
Okay, so you really wanna know, then?

00:15:38.910 --> 00:15:41.630
Yup, about everything!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.250
Fill 'er up, if you ya could.

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:47.000
What's he planning to do 
with all this gasoline?

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.420
Afraid I'm gonna go starting fires?

00:15:48.420 --> 00:15:49.330
No, I didn't mean...

00:15:49.960 --> 00:15:51.130
Right away, then.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:32.330
What's the matter, you scared?

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:35.460
It's so incredible! It's really 
something, hey Ol' Sab?

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:37.470
This is what Ijitsu looks like, huh!

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:40.290
Yup.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.080
But this isn't everything.

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:57.130
What the heck kind of landing did you pull?

00:16:57.130 --> 00:16:59.460
How do you go and lose just your engine?

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:05.040
Got it! There's my plug!

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:06.920
Now I just need a plug cord-

00:17:07.290 --> 00:17:11.430
Natsuo always went on and on about
how wiring was an art, huh.

00:17:11.430 --> 00:17:12.920
Not that I followed one bit.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:16.380
Reona gave me this scarf, didn't she?

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:18.960
Sorry I gotta do this, but thanks, Reona!

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:27.040
Hup!

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:37.880
Ol' Sa-!

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:40.210
I would like your assistance.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:42.830
Yeah, and what would I get for it?

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.580
Anything you desire.

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.080
I don't need a damn thing.

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:48.920
I've got no plans to start any
new research and development now.

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:50.040
That's a no, then?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.460
Did you not hear me?

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:53.710
You've never thought about going back?

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:57.580
I'll be around again.

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.920
What a cute little girl.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:04.670
Your daughter?

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:05.380
Never seen her.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:07.000
Yes, he has! I'm Kylie!

00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:07.600
Quiet!

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:09.790
Go on home.

00:18:11.580 --> 00:18:13.000
And never come back here again.

00:18:26.790 --> 00:18:28.290
Ol' Sab!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:31.750
That's not fair!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.290
Don't leave without me!

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:35.790
I still haven't seen anything yet!

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.790
Ordinarily the route would pass
between Gadoll and Rahama.

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:43.630
12 hours after her scheduled arrival time,
we began our search in this area.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:45.640
It has now been 44 hours.

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:50.250
I got in touch with Julia, but 
she says Kylie left just fine.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:53.480
Though she implied that perhaps
she ran off with all the money.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.000
Kylie of all people?

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:56.140
Not a chance.

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:58.250
She's never really been in it for the money.

00:18:58.250 --> 00:18:59.500
She'd never-ever!

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:02.250
I'm sure she's still 
toughing it out somewhere!

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.580
Of course, she is.

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:07.790
Well let's put together a 
more thorough search, then.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.130
It's roughly six AM.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:12.250
Skies are clear.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:15.630
Wind is blowing in at two 
khrill from the south east.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:16.460
Perfect flying weather.

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:23.250
Like it or not, do or die, 
I only got one shot at this!

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:35.040
All right!

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:25.700
Hold it steady.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:30.160
You can only pull on that yoke 
once you hit 50 kilo-khrill.

00:20:34.870 --> 00:20:36.330
C'mon!

00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:53.250
You don't fly a plane, they fly on their own.

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.420
All a pilot needs to do is follow its lead.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:04.500
I'm gonna go see all the 
stuff I haven't seen yet.

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:06.380
Bye-bye, Ol' Sab.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:16.170
Huh?

00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:17.040
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:21.800
Kylie!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:38.790
Jeez, where the heck were you?

00:21:39.170 --> 00:21:40.790
I'm astounded.

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:42.380
Is our payment safe?

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:45.250
Uh-oh, looks like someone's got a boo-boo.

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:48.000
I'll be waiting for your debriefing!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.920
It's good to be home.

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:08.580
Ano sora o jiyuu ni kakenukete mitai to

00:22:08.580 --> 00:22:12.420
Hanasaki no kaze ni negai o noseta

00:22:12.420 --> 00:22:16.330
Akogare ga keshiki o tsukutteiku

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:20.750
Ano toki no kaze wa genki kanaa

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:29.080
Nan no tame ni tatakau no kana

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:33.130
Koko ni iru riyuu wa nan darou?

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:41.380
Toikaketa sora wa kotaenai kedo

00:22:42.080 --> 00:22:49.040
Bokura wa tsubasa o motteiru

00:22:49.040 --> 00:22:53.750
Haruka kanata nageki no shuuchakuten

00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:58.000
Mitsuketa monogataritachi

00:22:58.000 --> 00:23:05.750
Kono sora wa dare ni mo ubaenai

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:10.460
Boku wa kakeru nanimo kowakunai yo

00:23:10.460 --> 00:23:17.630
Shiawase nara koko ni aru yo

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.460
Preview

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:37.580
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"Blood for a Nazarin Pound"!

00:23:38.210 --> 00:23:40.960
Blood for a Nazarin Pound
